<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emmerich am Rhein</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emmerich am Rhein is a town on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> border. It received town rights in 1233, later belonged to the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> and was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>. Largely destroyed in 1944–1945, it is crossed by the Rhine bridge at Emmerich, the longest suspension bridge in Germany.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emmerich-am-rhein.jpg" alt="Emmerich am Rhein" width="320" height="128" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raimond Spekking · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emmerich_am_Rhein_Osten.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
